# TERRAIN-BIND: the landscape's G-buffer program reads WorldParameters (Common/WeatherSnow.glslh, FIELD-WINTER) and takes
# it from the one applier every lit material gets its scene groups from (SceneFrameBinding::ApplyTo by the template's
# SceneReads; TerrainRenderer::ApplySceneFrame, 24ff76541). The p9base "no ground" frame was a stale Release binary
# (06:57, FPS-MAC p8 source without 24ff76541) run against the runtime-compiled shaders that already read the table.
# Headless Release (build/Bin/Release/Editor), the FPS-MAC eye view:
#   Editor --project Projects/Desert/Desert.deproj --scene Content/Scenes/<scene> --camera 0,170,2500
#          --look 0.15,-0.03,-1 --shot <dir>/<frame>.png --shot-frames 120
Проект Projects/Desert/Desert.deproj --scene Content/Scenes/FIELD_Barn.desce
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Position 0,170,2500
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0.15,-0.03,-1
Тогда barn_ground FIELD_Barn from the eye: the ground is drawn under the grass to the horizon, no sky through the ground; editor.log has no "filled by neither"
Когда run Scene "Open Scene FIELD_Barn_Winter.desce"
Тогда barn_ground_winter FIELD_Barn_Winter from the eye: the ground is drawn and lies white under snow, no sky through it; no "filled by neither"
